------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ml_kem_braid/crypto/_curve25519/curve/ contains Signal's curve25519 reference C
(vendored from python-axolotl-curve25519), licensed GPLv3. This code is
compiled into and linked with the _curve25519 extension module. Because that
GPLv3 code is combined into the shipped binary, the project as a whole is
distributed under the GPLv3 (GPL-3.0-or-later); this is the resolution of the
previously-deferred GPLv3-vs-MIT question.

Other Python dependencies (kyber-py, cryptography, pycryptodome, reedsolo,
fastapi, uvicorn, httpx, pydantic) are distributed under their own permissive
licenses (MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0), which are compatible with GPLv3.
